  "implementation": [
    "Schema98 adds immutable batch provenance and a frozen target Connection/generation set to the shared operation ledger. Policy, preferences, topology revision, reconciliation reference and queued work commit atomically. Exact policy replay returns the original receipt/reference without queuing another batch or resetting the latest policy.",
    "An optional typed codec_reconciliation reference separates completed Session policy acceptance from media execution. Reconciliation metadata uses current original member/manager/recipient authority and aggregate counts, without exposing private Connection IDs. Noncompleted operations keep result absent, preserving the shared ledger contract.",
    "NativeSessionCodecRead acquires the complete current manager/target footprint once, then resolves again under it. It checks the accepted latest policy, frozen exact target generation/preferences/deadline, original manager credential and member epoch, current named management and recipient authority, independently current original target connection.offer rights, key/Device/Endpoint/lifetime and observed credential epoch. It does not borrow stream.subscribe or target-initiated connection.update authority.",
    "One exact native-stream child effect is durably marked before possible IO. Changed IDs cannot create another attempt for the same target, and concurrent controls or stale revision/epoch/policy refuse. A sealed consumed lease captures historical codec results; no-change preserves stream revision, while changed results record exact binding metadata and revision. Native effect confirmation, readiness metadata, target outcome and batch completion commit together.",
    "Cancellation stops unstarted work and retains submitted uncertainty. Superseding policy skips only unstarted old work. Periodic SQL reconciliation recovers lost wake hints without reconstructing a lease or resubmitting IO. Restart settles old queued work unavailable and preserves submitted work unknown; an old-runtime capture cannot be reused.",
    "Nine controlled tests prove separate limited manager and peer credentials (with neither stream.subscribe nor target connection.update borrowed), atomic failure rollback, immutable replay/latest-policy ordering, forged job refusal, once-only child admission, no-change revision, current manager revocation, cancellation before/after submission, restart cases, current rotated source epoch, and captured success recovery after a recording failure without another effect.",
    "The164 native-stream/Session-control methods include those nine cases; four schema/backup tests and two receipt/snapshot recovery tests add up to170 distinct Rust methods. Current default server compilation,225 published schema vectors, HTTP reference regeneration, formatting and unchanged source hashes also pass."
  ],
